With https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/commit/6a47481ca48415515a51c701864c244f08da1c0d merged, the following helper function should simplify the job of porting a WORKSPACE macro to Bzlmod by turning it into a module extension and using `module_ctx.extension_metadata` to let Bazel generate fixup commands for out-of-date `use_repo` calls. @Wyverald and I are looking for an accessible home for such a function.

This snippet currently requires using `last_green`, but the features will be in 6.2.0. The fixup commands require a version of buildozer including https://github.com/bazelbuild/buildtools/commit/a3f457d62dd935c306e277abc33d38c50478fcf3.

```starlark
def wrap_macro(macro, *, dev_dependency = False):
    def impl(module_ctx):
        macro()
        return module_ctx.extension_metadata(
            root_module_direct_deps = [] if dev_dependency else "all",
            root_module_direct_dev_deps = "all" if dev_dependency else [],
        )
    return module_extension(impl)
```
